</style>
<h2>Asobi 1.0 (build 968)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Attachments on notes.</b> The paperclip in the composer (or a file dropped on it) puts an image, a movie, audio, a PDF or text with the note &#8212; or as the note. Each shows as a tile; click it for the viewer, with Download and Reveal in Finder. Files travel with the session and in a package. (Sharing them to other seats, replies with files, and the PDF report follow.)</li>
<li><b>A web reviewer's voice note keeps its audio on your Mac.</b> It was transcribed and discarded, so the note had words but no play control; now it plays here like your own.</li>
<li><b>Pause and resume a voice note</b> with the same button, on both platforms; the web's control shows &#9654; / &#9208;.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
